   STORAGE_PROCESS_TYPE_CD             VARCHAR(10)     COMMENT 'This code denotes a type of storage process that summarizes storage process steps in order to define complex processes for putaway, stock removal, and warehouse internal movements (e.g. a goods receipt process may contain the storage process steps for unloading and putaway, whereas a goods issue process may contain the storage process steps for stock removal, packing, staging and loading). Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   IS_HANDLING_UNIT_PROCESS_COMPLETE_FG BOOLEAN         COMMENT 'A flag that shows whether all the planned process for the Handling Unit are complete or not. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   STOCK_MANAGING_ORG_CD               VARCHAR(32)     COMMENT 'This is the code of the stock managing organization which is in charge of moving stock within the warehouse, sending it to customers or disposing it. 
            This code is introduced because there is a SAP functionality which allows multiple parties (organizations) to use the same warehouse for storing their stock. 
            Warehouses, used by Lidl E-Commerce (LEC) will always have the value LEC populated in this field as they are used solely by LEC. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   STORAGE_TYPE_CD                     VARCHAR(10)     COMMENT 'A storage type is a physical space characterized by its function in the warehouse where Handling Units could be stored e.g. Bulk Storage Area, General Storage Area etc. A storage type consists of one or more storage units.',
