   WH_TASK_PROCESSING_TYPE_CD          VARCHAR(10)     COMMENT 'A technical field to describe the process of a task. e.g. Fragile items should be picked carefully.',
   IS_HANDLING_UNIT_SYSTEM_CREATED_FG  BOOLEAN         COMMENT 'A flag that shows whether the Handling Unit was created automatically by the system or not. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   ITEM_DEFECT_CD                      VARCHAR(5)      COMMENT 'A code that shows if there is any defected item present on Handling Unit and what kind of a defect there is. e.g partially damaged or completely damaged and so on. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   HANDLING_UNIT_CREATE_TMSP           TIMESTAMP_TZ    COMMENT 'The point in time when the Handling Unit was created. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   PACK_SIZE_CD                        VARCHAR(10)     COMMENT 'The code for the size of the package.',
   PACK_GROUP_CD                       VARCHAR(10)     COMMENT 'The code for the group of the packages. e.g. there could 3 different kinds of cartons varying either in size or type but they could be grouped under Pallets.',
   HANDLING_UNIT_STATUS_CD             VARCHAR(5)      COMMENT 'The status of the Handling Unit to see if it is available, deleted or completed. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   IS_HANDLING_UNIT_HIGHEST_HIERARCHY_FG BOOLEAN         COMMENT 'A flag that shows whether the Handling Unit belongs to the heighest hierarchy or not. The hierarchy is as follows Bin > Palett > Cartons. When its true then it refers to Bins. When both hierarchy flags (highest and lowest) are false, it refers to Pallets. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   IS_HANDLING_UNIT_LOWEST_HIERARCHY_FG BOOLEAN         COMMENT 'A flag that shows whether the Handling Unit belongs to the lowest hierarchy or not. The hierarchy is as follows Bin > Palett > Cartons. When its true, it refers to Cartons. When both hierarchy flags (highest and lowest) are false, it refers to Pallets. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
   IS_WH_TASK_ASSIGNED_FG              BOOLEAN         COMMENT 'A flag that shows whether the goods on the Handling Unit have a warehouse task assigned to them or not. Same for all stock items transported on a handling unit with the same handling log id.',
